 5. DATA PRIVACY AND SESSION HANDLING
===============================================================================
  Cardinal is designed to manage apps and store their data locally. The
  Cardinal runtime stores its login settings, app configuration, app data,
  database files, logs, and local certificate under its configured data
  directory.

  A. LOCAL DATA: Cardinal's own control-plane login sessions are held in
     memory. App data and logs are stored locally by Cardinal.
  B. APP RESPONSIBILITY: Apps run as child processes and may store or transmit
     data independently. Review each app and its configuration; Cardinal's
     local API and data handling do not guarantee the behavior of installed
     apps.
  C. NO INCLUDED ANALYTICS: The Cardinal source export does not include an
     advertising analytics or data-broker service.
